# Future Work — Portfolio Site

A running list of planned improvements. Roughly ordered by priority within each section.

## 1. Dark / Light Mode
- Add a dark/light theme toggle (leverage existing styles/variables.css).
- Move hardcoded colors (e.g. tag/link backgrounds in portfolioEntry.js) into CSS custom properties.
- Persist user choice (localStorage) and respect prefers-color-scheme on first visit.

## 2. About / Skills Section
- Split the home page: keep a short introduction/hero, and break the rest of the
  bio into a dedicated "About" section.
- Add a distinct Skills block (languages, tools, frameworks) — grouped badges
  rather than prose so it can be scanned quickly.

## 3. Pinned / Featured Projects
- Pick 2-3 strongest projects (e.g. IGS Incubator, Formal Modeling Research) and
  give them prominence above the full portfolio list.
- Consider a "featured" flag in entries.json / entry .json files to drive this.

## 4. Recognition / Awards Section
- Add a dedicated section to highlight awards and recognition (we have a couple
  worth calling out — e.g. the IGS award).
- Include short context for each: what it was, when, and why it mattered.

## 5. Favicon Polish & Open Graph Meta Tags
- Clean up / add a proper favicon set (already referencing images/logo.png).
- Add Open Graph + Twitter Card meta tags to each page so shared links unfurl
  nicely on LinkedIn / social (title, description, image, url).

## 6. Alt Tags & Accessibility
- Add descriptive alt text to all images (several <img> currently lack it —
  home, contact, portfolio entry bodies).
- Add keyboard focus states, semantic landmarks, and check color contrast.
- Verify heading order and fix the unclosed <ul> in contact/contact.html.

## 7. Portfolio Narrative Cleanup
- Clean up the narrative structure of portfolio entries for consistency.
- Apply a consistent problem -> approach -> result structure across entries.
- Proofread/copyedit (a few typos exist, e.g. "Probablistic", "humdifier",
  "compoenents").
